# Cursor Rules Management

> ⚠️ **CRITICAL: NEVER modify cursor rules directly in individual repositories.**
> All cursor rules are managed centrally in the `sre-cursor-rules` repository.

## Centralized Rule Management

Playtomic uses a centralized approach to manage Cursor AI rules across all SRE repositories.

### How It Works

1. **Source of Truth:** All cursor rules live in [`syltek/sre-cursor-rules`](https://github.com/syltek/sre-cursor-rules)
2. **Automatic Sync:** A GitHub Actions workflow syncs rules to all configured repositories
3. **Rule Mappings:** Different repository types receive different sets of rules based on `config/rule-mappings.yaml`

### Do's and Don'ts

| ✅ DO | ❌ DON'T |
|-------|----------|
| Modify rules in `sre-cursor-rules` repo | Modify `.cursor/rules/` in other repositories |
| Create PRs to `sre-cursor-rules` for new rules | Create cursor rule files directly in project repos |
| Follow the rule format with YAML frontmatter | Skip the sync process |
| Update `rule-mappings.yaml` for new rules | Assume rules will stay if added locally |

### Adding or Modifying Rules

1. Clone `sre-cursor-rules` repository
2. Create/modify rules in the `.cursor/rules/` directory
3. Update `config/rule-mappings.yaml` if adding new rule categories
4. Update `config/repo-mappings.yaml` if adding new repositories
5. Create a PR with proper Linear task ID
6. Once merged, rules sync automatically to all configured repositories
